### Writing rules

1. **Write simply. Keep technical terms.** Short sentences. One idea per sentence. Active voice. Gloss technical terms on first use.

2. **Link everything.** Every Deep Dive needs a direct URL. Every wiki reference needs a relative link.

3. **Show the architecture.** Use text-based HLD diagrams (box-and-arrow) when it adds clarity.

4. **Calibrate depth to tier.** Tier 1: 4–6 paragraphs + mechanism + research angle. Tier 2: 2–4 paragraphs. Tier 3: Quick Hit.

5. **Be opinionated and specific.** Name the tension. Name the prior paper. Take a position.

6. **Future implications must be falsifiable.** Name a specific claim and timeframe.

7. **Connect before you summarize.** The unique value of this wiki is accumulated context. Use it.

8. **Write as a second brain.** Every Deep Dive should reference prior wiki knowledge. A digest that could have been written without reading any prior pages has failed.

